1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,940
In this Sales workflow, we will create a
customer order, add its articles, review

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:09,000
availability, and confirm the order for the next department.

3
00:00:11,708 --> 00:00:14,028
Step one: Create a Sales Order.

4
00:00:14,588 --> 00:00:18,108
In Explorer, open Sales, then Sales Orders.

5
00:00:18,848 --> 00:00:20,828
Choose New and select Sales Order.

6
00:00:23,417 --> 00:00:25,417
Accept the generated order number.

7
00:00:25,977 --> 00:00:27,837
The new customer order starts in Draft.

8
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:34,523
Select the customer and the delivery and invoice addresses.

9
00:00:35,303 --> 00:00:40,243
Enter the customer reference, then review
the order date, currency and price list.

10
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:45,337
Step two: Add the order lines.

11
00:00:46,077 --> 00:00:47,297
Add an article from the Library.

12
00:00:47,957 --> 00:00:53,617
This example orders four pieces at twenty-two
euros each, for a total of eighty-eight

13
00:00:53,637 --> 00:00:55,957
euros. Save and close the order.

14
00:00:58,542 --> 00:01:01,122
Step three: Review stock availability.

15
00:01:01,822 --> 00:01:04,522
Open Stock availability from the Lines tab.

16
00:01:05,042 --> 00:01:08,002
Four pieces are required and none are available.

17
00:01:08,822 --> 00:01:10,882
Review the shortage before confirming.

18
00:01:13,458 --> 00:01:15,538
Step four: Confirm the order.

19
00:01:16,298 --> 00:01:18,458
Select the saved Sales Order in Explorer.

20
00:01:19,498 --> 00:01:23,378
Choose Change State, set the new state to Confirmed, then apply.

21
00:01:26,125 --> 00:01:27,865
Check that the transition succeeded.

22
00:01:28,745 --> 00:01:34,785
In this example, confirmation creates a material
requirement for the uncovered four pieces.

23
00:01:35,545 --> 00:01:37,945
Hand that demand to Procurement.

24
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:43,120
Pause for details and follow the full guide.
